      'a spinning wheel mechanises the twisting a large drive wheel turned by hand or by a foot treadle is connected by a drive band to a small spindle or a flyer and bobbin assembly so it spins fast and continuously the spinner just drafts and feeds fibre in and the wheel adds twist a flyer wheel also winds the yarn on automatically as you go',
