      'combining them stockinette stocking stitch is knit every right side row all vs on the front smooth curls at the edges garter stitch is knit every row bumpy and flat on both sides ribbing alternates columns of knit and purl and is very stretchy sideways seed or moss stitch alternates knit and purl in a checkerboard and lies flat',
